Le samedi 30 janvier 2016 09:31:10 UTC, la .tamar. a =C3=A9crit :
>
> Coi.
>
> I gave up learning lojban a while ago because I didn't have anyone I woul=
d=20
> be able to learn it with, but recently I got some new friends who want to=
=20
> learn. I decided that at the start I would teach them to speak saying eve=
ry=20
> terminator so that we get used to the idea of them being there, however I=
=20
> noticed that it is inconsistent as to whether or not la is terminated by =
ku=20
> or if it has no terminator. For example in la camxes grammar parser addin=
g=20
> a ku to the end of a sumti starting with la generates an error unless you=
=20
> use the experimental grammar version. My question therefore is, is using =
ku=20
> as a terminator experimental? and should I teach them that it is the=20
> terminator for la, or shouldn't I?
>
>
Officially, {la} followed by selbri has an elidable terminator {ku}, but=20
{la} followed by cmevla does not have a terminator. It is because a brivla=
=20
following {la ca selbri} can be included the {la}-structure, while a brivla=
=20
following {la cmevlas} cannot be a part of the {la}-structure.

I recommend using camxes for teaching beginners, not the=20
canxes-experimental that was deteriorated by la gleki. Although I rather=20
welcome improvement of the grammar, most of the ideas of new grammar are=20
not yet discussed by BPFK, and some of the ideas may be not going to be=20
agreed by it. As for actual reading or listening of existing texts in=20
experimental grammar, I prepared some versions of parsers that are suitable=
=20
to them. See the instruction of the versions for detail:
https://mw.lojban.org/papri/zantufa

For example,=20

- use maftufa for reading lo se manci te makfa pe la oz:
https://mw.lojban.org/papri/maftufa
http://selpahi.de/oz_plain.html

- use zantufa for reading the new version of {la .teris. ku noi tigra cu=20
stuvi'e lo barda tcadu} or listening my song {lo no valsi}:
http://guskant.github.io/gerna_cipra/zantufa-1.11.html
https://mw.lojban.org/papri/la_.teris._ku_noi_tigra_cu_stuvi'e_lo_barda_tca=
du
https://vimeo.com/141602354

- use maltufa for reading the old version of {la teris po'u lo tirxu cu=20
vitke zi'o le barda tcadu} and most of good old texts:
http://guskant.github.io/gerna_cipra/maltufa-1.1.html
https://mw.lojban.org/papri/la_.teris._po'u_lo_tirxu_cu_vitke_zi'o_le_barda=
_tcadu

-use zantufa-cekitaujoibus for reading {ka catra lo verba}:
http://guskant.github.io/gerna_cipra/zantufa-1-cekitaujoibu.html
http://danmo-rozgu.github.io/kacatraloverba.html

mu'o

